        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420-a1">

                <pb facs="0753" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg683"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Prieto to Mr. Cayetano Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States of Mexico</hi><lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Tombstone, Ariz.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1883-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 24, 1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I this day address the secretary of foreign relations as follows:</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inform you that, according to the newspapers of this city,
                    extracts from which, with translations, are herewith inclosed, small parties of
                    Apaches have been leaving the San Carlos Reservation and entering the State of
                    Sonora since the early part of this month. According to advices received from
                    that State, they have already committed depredations. General Crook, in whose
                    command said reservation is, has been informed of this by telegraph, but I have
                    not yet learned that any steps have been taken to check these movements. It is
                    difficult to see why, when the American Government has so many troops on the
                    Indian reservations in this Territory, it allows the savages to commit all sorts
                    of outrages in our Republic, after having been driven out of which by our
                    troops, they quietly return to their reservations.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to transcribe the foregoing to you for your information, and for
                    such other purposes as you may think proper.</p>
                <p>I remain, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DIAZ PRIETO.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
